    "released_at": "2026-09-28",
    "changelog": "Where a grocery is kept is its Location now, the same place its shelf label lists: the separate Storage field is gone, a scan that reads Pantry files the item into your Pantry, and the Storage you had already set moves over on this update. Earlier: Wine has its own collection now, so a scanned bottle files there when both are installed; Groceries no longer claims the word wine. Earlier: Call them what you call them: items, groceries or pantry items. Pick the word when you install, or change it later in the table's settings, and every label says it.",
    "name": "Groceries",
    "description": "Turn inventory + lists into a kitchen system: track food with expiry + storage fields, an auto grocery list on low-stock/expiry, restock on check-off.",
    "author": "Cobblr",
    "features": [
      {
        "key": "kitchen-places",
        "name": "Set up your kitchen",
        "question": "Shall we set up a Fridge and a Freezer you can file things into?",
        "description": "Adds Kitchen with a Fridge, Freezer and Pantry inside it, so you can put a label on each and scan things straight in. If you already have a Kitchen these go inside the one you have, and nothing already in it is moved. Decline and grocery tracking works exactly the same.",
        "default": true,
        "provides_locations": [
          {
            "name": "Kitchen",
            "kind": "area",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "Fridge",
                "kind": "container"
              },
              {
                "name": "Freezer",
                "kind": "container"
              },
              {
                "name": "Pantry",
                "kind": "container"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
